  "notes": {
    "calloutNotes": {
      "fill": "blue",
      "maxH": 520,
      "text": "Grouped callouts — what it takes to ship\n\n1. Cluster by lap fraction from trackProgress (e.g. < 1.5% of a lap), not pixel distance. Recompute 1–2×/s, not per frame.\n2. Hysteresis: join < 1.2%, split > 2%, hold a layout ≥ 2 s, or boxes flicker with estimated positions.\n3. Placement: outward normal at the cluster centre (like corner.angle), try a few distances out then in, reject boxes hitting the track polyline, other boxes or corner numbers.\n4. Leader line end follows the dots in the existing rAF loop; the box stays put.\n5. Pit cars excluded; lapped cars marked; mobile falls back to plain circles.\n\nQuick v1: fixed-normal placement, accept occasional overlap.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": 1180,
      "y": 7424
    },
    "mobileNote": {
      "fill": "teal",
      "maxH": 560,
      "text": "Mobile rules (< 768 px)\n\n• Top bar becomes one row: logo, session, Live chip. A second row keeps lap/clock, weather and track status always visible.\n• The 6 tabs move to a bottom bar: Live, Map, Messages, Strategy, More. More opens Weather, Standings, Schedule, Settings, Help.\n• Tables drop to the columns that fit 390 px; tap a row for the full detail (sectors, stints).\n• Side panels (push laps, long runs, incidents) become a strip or a segment under the main content.\n• Fluid pages (Weather, Standings, Settings, Home, Schedule, Help) reflow without a separate layout.",
      "w": 400,
      "x": 3760,
      "y": 4580
    },
